  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Desarrollo de actividades comunitarias para la reduccin de la desigualdad en la vida de las nias, adolescentes y jvenes indgenas durante dos aos en Raxruh y Chisec, A.V.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young Indigenous women in rural Guatemala have few opportunities to develop skills that enable them to fully contribute to the development of their communities. The IAF supports community-led approaches to civic engagement and human rights. IAF grantee partner Organizacin No Gubernamental Nalebak ONG (NALEBAK) empowers young women and adolescents in the communities of Chisec and Raxruh, Alta Verapaz, to address gender inequality, strengthen their leadership skills, reduce gender-based violence, and improve the food security of their families. Grant activities include popular education and leadership workshops, establishing safe spaces in the community, and creating community gardens to promote food security.This grant is part of the IAF&apos;s Women INvesting in Growth and Security (WINGS) initiative to empower women as business and community leaders and part of the IAF&apos;s efforts to address the root causes of irregular migration in Central America.</narrative>
  </description>
